<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.3.1: Creating a Pictorial Representation of Exponential Growth</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01275</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.3.1: Creating a Pictorial Representation of Exponential Growth</md:title>
    <md:uuid>1c424007-496c-4c22-affb-d9b0a3142890</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">
          <media alt="Bacteria viewed through a microscope.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_05_02_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <para id="para-00002">There are some bacteria in a dish. Every hour, each bacterium splits into 3 bacteria.</para>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00001">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00003">This diagram shows a bacterium in hour 0 and then hour 1. Draw what happens in hours 2 and 3.</para>
            <para id="para-00004">
                      <media alt="The picture shows 1 bacterium (an irregular polygon with a double outline and light blue inside) for hour 0, then an arrow to the right, then 3 bacteria for hour 1.">
                  <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_05_02_02.png"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
            <para id="para-00005">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00006">Your answers may vary, but here is an example:</para>
            <para id="para-00007">
                      <media alt="Illustration of bacteria growth.">
                  <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_05_02_03.png"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      


        <exercise id="_895d2b51-784f-48d1-a2e9-1164d1863071" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00008">How many bacteria are there in hour 2?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00009">Correct! There are 9 bacteria in hour 2.</para>
            <para id="para-00010">The correct answer is: There are 9 bacteria in hour 2.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="c21693f7-580f-4dcb-bdac-d807f41567bc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00011">How many bacteria are there in hour 3?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00012">Correct! There are 27 bacteria in hour 3.</para>
            <para id="para-00013">The correct answer is: There are 27 bacteria in hour 3.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

    </section>
  </content>
